proof:
Proof. Put \(k=\overline{\mathbb F}_q\) and let \(\sigma:k\to k\), \(\sigma(c)=c^{q^m}\). For a scheme \(Z\) over \(\mathbb F_{q^m}\) write \(F_Z=(\operatorname{id}_{Z_k}\times\operatorname{Spec}\sigma)^*\) for the \(q^m\)-power arithmetic Frobenius acting on \(H^*_{\mathrm{\acute et}}(Z_k,\mathbb Q_\ell)\); this is a \(\mathbb Q_\ell\)-linear automorphism of each cohomology group, because \(\sigma\) is an automorphism of \(k\) over \(\mathbb F_{q^m}\) and \(H^n_{\mathrm{\acute et}}(Z_k,\mathbb Q_\ell)\) is contravariantly functorial in \(Z_k\).

Step 1: semisimplicity on the base curve \(C\). We apply [Spark/043be352939fa7b2/lemma_364] to the given data \((q=p^a,\ \ell\neq p,\ m\ge 1,\ C)\). All of its hypotheses are literally hypotheses of the target lemma: \(q=p^a\) is a prime power, \(\ell\neq p\) is prime, \(m\ge1\), and \(C\) is a smooth projective geometrically connected curve over \(\mathbb F_{q^m}\). Its conclusion is that the \(q^m\)-power arithmetic Frobenius \((\operatorname{id}_{C_k}\times\operatorname{Spec}\sigma)^*=F_C\) on \(H^n_{\mathrm{\acute et}}(C_{\overline{\mathbb F}_q},\mathbb Q_\ell)\) is semisimple, that is diagonalizable over \(\overline{\mathbb Q}_\ell\), for every integer \(n\ge0\). In particular \(F_C\) is semisimple on \(H^n_{\mathrm{\acute et}}(C_k,\mathbb Q_\ell)\) for every \(n\ge0\).

Step 2: passage to the projective bundle. We apply [Spark/9827c89e17d0e461/ca8fad] with \(Y=C\), with \(\mathcal E\) the given vector bundle, and with \(\rho\) its rank. We check its hypotheses one by one:
(i) \(C\) is a smooth projective geometrically connected variety of pure dimension over \(\mathbb F_{q^m}\): it is a smooth projective geometrically connected curve, hence of pure dimension \(1\);
(ii) \(\mathcal E\) is a vector bundle of rank \(\rho\ge1\) on \(C\) defined over \(\mathbb F_{q^m}\), as assumed in the target;
(iii) \(\pi:P=\mathbf P_C(\mathcal E)\to C\) is the projective bundle of one-dimensional quotients, as assumed in the target;
(iv) the \(q^m\)-power arithmetic Frobenius \((\operatorname{id}\times\operatorname{Spec}\sigma)^*\), \(\sigma(c)=c^{q^m}\), is semisimple on \(H^n_{\mathrm{\acute et}}(C_k,\mathbb Q_\ell)\) for every \(n\ge0\), which is precisely Step 1.
The conclusion of [Spark/9827c89e17d0e461/ca8fad] is that the \(q^m\)-power arithmetic Frobenius is semisimple on \(H^n_{\mathrm{\acute et}}(P_k,\mathbb Q_\ell)\) for every \(n\ge0\), and that its scalar extension to \(\overline{\mathbb Q}_\ell\) is diagonalizable.

Step 3: identification of the operators. The Frobenius operator appearing in [Spark/9827c89e17d0e461/ca8fad] is \((\operatorname{id}\times\operatorname{Spec}\sigma)^*\) with \(\sigma(c)=c^{q^m}\), i.e. exactly the operator \((\operatorname{id}_{P_k}\times\operatorname{Spec}\sigma)^*\) of the target lemma; likewise the base operator in Step 1 is exactly \((\operatorname{id}_{C_k}\times\operatorname{Spec}\sigma)^*\). Hence no comparison of two different Frobenius actions is required, and the conclusion of Step 2 is literally the conclusion of the target lemma: \((\operatorname{id}_{P_k}\times\operatorname{Spec}\sigma)^*\) is semisimple on \(H^n_{\mathrm{\acute et}}(P_k,\mathbb Q_\ell)\) for every integer \(n\ge0\), and its scalar extension to \(\overline{\mathbb Q}_\ell\) is diagonalizable.

Remark (the two formulations agree). For a \(\mathbb Q_\ell\)-linear operator \(T\) on a finite-dimensional \(\mathbb Q_\ell\)-vector space \(V\), semisimplicity of \(T\) is equivalent to diagonalizability of \(T\otimes\operatorname{id}\) on \(V\otimes_{\mathbb Q_\ell}\overline{\mathbb Q}_\ell\): indeed \(T\) is semisimple iff its minimal polynomial is squarefree, iff the minimal polynomial of \(T\otimes\operatorname{id}\) (the same polynomial) splits with distinct roots over the algebraically closed field \(\overline{\mathbb Q}_\ell\), iff \(T\otimes\operatorname{id}\) is diagonalizable. Thus the two assertions in the target statement are in fact one and the same condition; in any case [Spark/9827c89e17d0e461/ca8fad] supplies both of them, so the target lemma is proved in full.
